{"availability":"available","full":"luke321/vault-graph","name":"vault-graph","description":"Interactive graph of an Obsidian vault as Obsidian community plugin.","category":"Other","language":"JavaScript","stars":267,"forks":19,"created":"2026-08-22T08:14:59Z","updated":"2026-10-06T21:46:03Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://community.obsidian.md/plugins/vault-graph","topics":[],"demo":"https://luke321.github.io/vault-graph/demo/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T04:29:40.136Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T04:29:40.136Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T04:29:40.136Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T04:29:40.136Z","stars":267,"forks":19}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Your whole vault as one disc. Every note is a dot; every top-level folder owns a wedge of the circle whose angle is its share of the vault. Notes fill concentric rings from the middle outwards, best-connected first, so the best-connected notes sit near the centre and leaves land on the rim.","The layout is deterministic, not force-directed. There is no simulation to settle and no seed to get lucky with: the same vault always draws the same picture, so the shape becomes something you can learn and recognise rather than a fresh tangle each time.","Ships as an Obsidian plugin and as a standalone HTML exporter — one page, two mounts, from the same source. The exporter writes a single self-contained offline file with no server and no network, which is how the graph reaches a phone."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/luke321/vault-graph/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"d3b2426d358f4c4515a4e0002020a6975860506e2b0f78e17c3b13a24d2951a8","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T04:29:40.284Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T04:29:40.284Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Your whole vault as one disc. Every note is a dot; every top-level folder owns a wedge of the circle whose angle is its share of the vault. Notes fill concentric rings from the middle outwards, best-connected first, so the best-connected notes sit near the centre and leaves land on the rim.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/luke321/vault-graph/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Nothing leaves your machine — it makes no network requests, collects nothing, and needs no account.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/luke321/vault-graph/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"d3b2426d358f4c4515a4e0002020a6975860506e2b0f78e17c3b13a24d2951a8","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/luke321/vault-graph/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T04:29:40.285Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-06T21:46:03Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/luke321/vault-graph/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T04:29:40.286Z","hash":"d3b2426d358f4c4515a4e0002020a6975860506e2b0f78e17c3b13a24d2951a8","originalBytes":28063,"storedBytes":28063,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["vault","one","folder","obsidian","scripts","graph","note","file","notes","same","own","src","what","nothing","page","ai-context","every","folders","node","open","plugin","rather","two","colour","out","them","engine","it.","links","each","path","row","there","bash","only","about","does","real","which","browser","default","inside","just","other","per","slot","source","they","top-level","whose","back","because","build","decisions","demo","exporter","html","name","unlinked","any","build-graph.mjs","click","colours","count","four","frontmatter","how","legend","live","main.js","reads","run","see","still","their","under","where","built","checks","design","eye","first","install","layout","like","measured","npm","over","runs","setting","settings","shape","share","smoke.mjs","three","vault-graph","vault-graph.html","wedge","whole","works","writes","another","before","button","cannot","check","code","comes","decision","disc","drives","else","files","fixtures","generat